{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":2,"timestamp":1786942204,"nonce":"26quJ5Odjzs4c+6f3GEUgehLs1Y=","title":"`createSource` is typed `Promise\u003cSource\u003e` for a handler that answers `SourceCreatedDTO`, and the one-time dialog drops the `webhook_url` it carries","was":"**What is wrong.** `createSource` is declared `Promise\u003cSource\u003e` at `web/src/api/endpoints.ts:463-465` and calls `postItem\u003cSource\u003e`, but the handler answers `SourceCreatedDTO` — `{source, ingest_token, token_prefix, webhook_url}` (`api/openapi/openapi.yaml:7569-7593`, `internal/sources/api/sources.go:200-208`), which is a different object with a `SourceDTO` nested inside it. The single call site compensates with a cast through `unknown`: `props.onCreated(created as unknown as SourceCreated)` at `web/src/features/settings/SourcesSection.tsx:542`. Two consequences follow. The generated contract types cannot check this path at all — `as unknown as` is precisely the cast that suspends them — and `webhook_url`, which the response carries and the operator needs, is never rendered: `TokenDialog` (`SourcesSection.tsx:759-781`) shows `ingest_token` and a copy button, and tells the reader to \"Point your Alertmanager's webhook receiver at oto's ingest URL for this source\" without giving the URL it was just handed."}]}